    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 honda civic is making this really loud squealing noise whenever i'm accelerating. i think it's coming from the engine area. can you explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a bad one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A faulty serpentine belt can cause a loud squealing noise when accelerating, especially if it's slipping. The serpentine belt, also known as a multi-vee belt, is a tensioner-driven belt that powers various engine components such as the alternator, air conditioning compressor, and power steering pump. If the belt is worn or broken, it can cause misalignment, friction, and vibration, resulting in the distinctive squealing or chirping sound you're experiencing.",
