    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so if it is the belt, is it just a matter of replacing it or could something else be causing it to slip? like is there anything else that would make it squeal like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While a worn or broken serpentine belt is a common culprit, there are other factors that can cause it to slip and result in a squealing noise. Oil leaks from engine mounts or the serpentine belt tensioner can also cause misalignment and resulting squeal. Additionally, serpentine belt squeal can also be caused by excessive engine worn bearings or an out-of-whack engine shaft alignment, which would require more extensive repairs.",
